 .TP
+.BI --since " TIME" \fR|\fI INDEX
+Search only the objects an MDT changelog says have changed, verifying each one
+against the live filesystem, so every other option keeps the meaning it has
+without this one. The result is a strict subset of the same search without
+.BR --since :
+narrowed, never different. An object that matches but has not changed does not
+appear, and neither does one that has been unlinked since it changed. A
+directory counts as changed only when a record is about the directory itself,
+not when an entry is created, removed or renamed in it, although that changes
+its mtime and ctime.
+.IP
+.I TIME
+is a duration back from now, written
+.IR N [ smhdwy ]
+.RB ( 30s ", " 30m ", " 2h ", " 7d ", " 2w ", " 1y ),
+a timestamp
+.RB ( 2026-08-25 ", " 2026-08-25T18:00 ),
+or an epoch second written explicitly as
+.BR @1787674596 .
+A bare integer is an
+.I INDEX
+into one MDT's changelog, which is what
+.BR lfs-changelog (1)
+takes, and is refused on a filesystem with more than one MDT unless
+.B --changelog
+names which log it indexes: a
+.I cr_index
+belongs to one MDT and names a different instant on each of them. Nothing else
+is accepted, because a number that could be either an index or an epoch second
+must not be guessed at.
+.IP
+Reading a changelog does not consume it and does not require a registered
+changelog user, but records exist only while some user is registered. The
+changelog device is readable by root alone by default, so an ordinary user
+gets
+.B EACCES
+from
+.BR --since ,
+.B --since-cookie
+and
+.BR --changelog
+alike. See
+.BR lfs-changelog (1).
+.TP
 .BR -s ", " --size
 File size is
 .I N
