+	 * named is enforced here, against the resolved pathname -- without it
+	 * "lfs find /mnt/lustre/a --since 2h" would answer for /mnt/lustre/b
+	 * as well.  And find_decide() does not read fp_pattern, fp_type,
+	 * fp_check_mdt_count or fp_hash_type, which a walk answers in
+	 * find_prefilter() before it, so this must too, or --since answers a
+	 * different set from the same find without it.  That is the one thing
+	 * this option promises not to do.
+	 */
+	if (!find_since_pick(st, rec, &named, alt, sizeof(alt),
